  "dunesModel": "Each of 16 directional arrows compacts one selected row or column of a 4x4 board. Fixed pillars split the line; physical stones keep their within-segment order and never merge. Strict snake readout and the complete exact target-hole set are both required. A changed compaction charges one lifetime move; no-ops are free. B restores exact prior stone IDs, cells and action focus without refunding charged moves or active time. A final-budget goal wins before move-limit loss, but the active 90-second deadline precedes input. This is a discrete layout puzzle; interpolation does not simulate physical collisions.",
